   "message": "Fix flaky ApplyLinkWrench topic tests (#3870)\n\nPersistentFromTopic and InstantaneousFromTopic publish wrench commands\nover gz-transport and then immediately step the server. Delivery is\nasynchronous and unacknowledged: HasConnections() only proves that\ndiscovery has paired the publisher with the subscriber, not that\nApplyLinkWrenchPrivate::OnWrench*() has run. The first iteration's\nPreUpdate can therefore take the system mutex before either message has\nbeen queued, so the ExternalWorldWrenchCmd component does not exist yet\nand the measured acceleration is still zero.\n\nReplace the wall-clock assumptions with condition-based waiting:\n\n* PersistentFromTopic steps the server until the published wrenches (and\n  later the clear commands) have actually taken effect, and only then\n  measures the 100 iterations it asserts on. This also removes the\n  arbitrary 300 ms sleep flagged by the existing \\todo, and adds the\n  missing discovery wait before checking pubClear.HasConnections().\n\n* InstantaneousFromTopic no longer requires the impulse to land on\n  iteration 1. It steps one iteration at a time until each wrench is\n  applied and asserts the real invariant: each wrench is applied in\n  exactly one time step, with the commanded value. The two commands are\n  tracked separately because they can be delivered on different\n  iterations.\n\nVerified on an idle machine and under `stress -c 16 -i 16`:\n\n  test                     before (8 cpu)   after (16 cpu)\n  FromSdf                   0/40 failures    0/160\n  PersistentFromTopic      33/40 failures    0/160\n  InstantaneousFromTopic   30/40 failures    0/160\n\nMutation-tested to confirm the relaxed assertions still catch real\nregressions: dropping persistent wrenches, ignoring clear requests,\napplying an instantaneous wrench every step, and halving the applied\nforce are all still detected.\n\nFixes #2727\n\nAssisted-By: Claude Opus 5 <claude-opus-5>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Jose Luis Rivero <jrivero@honurobotics.com>\nSigned-off-by: Addisu Z. Taddese <addisuzt@intrinsic.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Addisu Z. Taddese <addisuzt@intrinsic.ai>",
