 {
  "sha": "86a92e5bb03e12c8397f4979cf735f1995f23186",
  "node_id": "C_kwDOD0AxsdoAKDg2YTkyZTViYjAzZTEyYzgzOTdmNDk3OWNmNzM1ZjE5OTVmMjMxODY",
  "commit": {
   "author": {
    "name": "Carlos Ag\u00fcero",
    "email": "caguero@honurobotics.com",
    "date": "2026-08-24T16:02:24Z"
   },
   "committer": {
    "name": "GitHub",
    "email": "noreply@github.com",
    "date": "2026-08-24T16:02:24Z"
   },
   "message": "Compute the duck volume expectation from the mesh instead of a baked constant (#3912)\n\ngazebosim/gz-common#877 corrected mesh Volume() for meshes that are not star shaped about the origin, which changed the test duck's collider volume from 1.40186 to 1.18892 m^3 and broke INTEGRATION_buoyancy UniformWorldMovement against current gz-common. The fix now computes the expected volume from the collider mesh itself, and the duck's final height from the closed form rise under constant net buoyancy, so it tracks the mesh volume computation instead of baking its output. The same closed form reproduces the previous 171.4 m expectation from the previous volume.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nSigned-off-by: Carlos Ag\u00fcero <caguero@honurobotics.com>",
   "tree": {
    "sha": "5bbd4b96d9b7d151e844fac82ad7aeb75dc6a9f8",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gazebosim/gz-sim/git/trees/5bbd4b96d9b7d151e844fac82ad7aeb75dc6a9f8"
   },
   "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gazebosim/gz-sim/git/commits/86a92e5bb03e12c8397f4979cf735f1995f23186",
   "comment_count": 0,
   "verification": {
    "verified": true,
    "reason": "valid",
    "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjGsQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8o8QACpGQRQuQpfkn9fvrGt3w+J7\nCdZqHvBovuBD3mYLM6oCw6k+G4mUOmUfxpcWR06wdcqI6OVkkaBweRqHHrBfjBTV\n9FGKcw9DSknZ3yrt4ywRXkOAbZJ01Fgbsw+TBHG4Ik0VGg8HPzT7iow404uIkkCY\njZFOgjOaPAGVBMcyPdRhZRXLGgLiAogbX9jsMCXIGjwSsguQV6tsYjmdoonfsor+\nWflfQRe2O2F+3yFBbZPzVIX5ssed3sHmazkjGZb0l/cy5IuX6YoLxtNr+qpkbZD+\n7x0l/6SbGdjjC838W+/4BXp4OTeNIBStkGbsFNyGtq01IPNeWf6I48FB7dfA05NG\ndeLU+ti+1fV/cn+i8uYR7qqGICboV4RI8TQbKcgSATPciGhQLvV0u+WtUn6lj7MY\nKpaVoN/wx4tINsY8b5fw/GTCmRDVqCEIMEgNEzLy6ILREBFKmX9HmtAOZgdgyZEh\ndVoLz1RtnhR0O/Klhqowgd8SaDlun0Z6I9Hs5ZxJaAO3CEnaeiUe6UrIWsapqOPl\nc2lMofhBtlaguBGufCFffR17clBr/ub+zX+Yjozvv4wrEVOPMvosovk6OTR+9ROn\nZBUJFplursnFBn/pbD6m0X28OdqDml4SuCuU5NVcH1B/QDBwrlWfxQ3eKYL589QP\nnqxCijL/K/fsLNLWyQ6n\n=kf47\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
    "payload": "tree 5bbd4b96d9b7d151e844fac82ad7aeb75dc6a9f8\nparent c90378b7c5ca46f3419abc546d485b2248aa4675\nauthor Carlos Ag\u00fcero <caguero@honurobotics.com> 1787587344 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787587344 -0700\n\nCompute the duck volume expectation from the mesh instead of a baked constant (#3912)\n\ngazebosim/gz-common#877 corrected mesh Volume() for meshes that are not star shaped about the origin, which changed the test duck's collider volume from 1.40186 to 1.18892 m^3 and broke INTEGRATION_buoyancy UniformWorldMovement against current gz-common. The fix now computes the expected volume from the collider mesh itself, and the duck's final height from the closed form rise under constant net buoyancy, so it tracks the mesh volume computation instead of baking its output. The same closed form reproduces the previous 171.4 m expectation from the previous volume.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nSigned-off-by: Carlos Ag\u00fcero <caguero@honurobotics.com>",
    "verified_at": "2026-08-24T16:02:24Z"
   }
